<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Workflow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <Workflow> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW FILE, 2026-09-01. LOI__c had no workflow metadata before this change. W1 of the LOI
        approval cutover (agent-output/loi-approval-cutover-design.md), which moves the principal
        LOI approval OFF Opportunity.LOI_Approval and ONTO the LOI__c record itself. Direct sibling
        of workflows/Underwriting__c.workflow-meta.xml (2026-08-28) — same shape, same reasoning,
        different object.

        🔴 ONE FIELD UPDATE, NO WORKFLOW RULE, NO REJECTION FIELD UPDATE. The single update below
        is fired ONLY by the new approvalProcesses/LOI__c.LOI_Approval as its finalApprovalActions.
        Do not add a <rules> element: an active rule writing LOI_Status__c on an ordinary edit
        would fake an approval.

        🔴 NO REJECTION FIELD UPDATE, BY DESIGN — USER DECISION D-3, QUOTED: "The LOI stage will
        remain on Under review after rejection." There is no finalRejectionActions on the approval
        process and nothing here mirrors one. This is the ACCEPTED, DOCUMENTED loss of the retired
        Opportunity.LOI_Approval's Set_Stage_Underwriting rejection action, which rewound the deal
        a full stage (LOI -> Underwriting). That rewind is structurally unreachable from an
        approval parented by LOI__c (LOI__c.Opportunity__c is a Lookup, not Master-Detail — an
        approval process can field-update only its own record or a Master-Detail parent), and an
        Apex substitute was considered and deliberately NOT built — see
        LoiApprovalStampService.cls's own header for why (it would newly have to satisfy
        NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression and No_Backward_Stage_Movement, which the old
        approval's field update bypassed). On rejection the LOI simply stays at
        Stage__c = 'Under Review' and only the approval history records the decision.

        WHY THIS RECORD'S OWN FIELD, NOT THE PARENT'S. This is the child-object half of moving the
        approval onto LOI__c. The field update writes only this record's own field — required,
        because LOI__c.Opportunity__c is a Lookup, so an approval process on this object cannot
        field-update the parent Opportunity at all. The parent mirror (Opportunity.LOI_Approved__c)
        is written separately by flows/LOI_Approval_Sync.flow-meta.xml, entry-scoped on
        LOI_Status__c transitioning to 'Approved' (recordTriggerType = Update,
        doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria = true — both load-bearing, see that flow's own
        header and LoiApprovalStampService.cls's "THE TRIGGERING MARKER (D-4)" section for the
        251-record bulk callers this exact pair of settings keeps immune), calling
        LoiApprovalStampService.

        DEPLOY ORDER — LOAD-BEARING. This file must land in the SAME deploy as (or before)
        approvalProcesses/LOI__c.LOI_Approval.approvalProcess-meta.xml, which references the field
        update below BY NAME and cannot deploy otherwise — the same requirement
        Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval's header records at its own deploy-order note.
    -->
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>LOI_Status_Approved</fullName>
        <description>Final approval action of LOI__c.LOI_Approval. Sets LOI Status to Approved on this LOI record. Consumed by flows/LOI_Approval_Sync, which mirrors the transition onto the parent deal.</description>
        <field>LOI_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Approved</literalValue>
        <name>LOI Status Approved</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
</Workflow>
